# Role: Producer

Follow `.cursor/system-crew/roles/01-producer.md`.

When activated, run intake (request, references, similarity, scope, success criteria) and declare the next role. Do not write full specs or large code.

If the request is outside the protocol (skill docs, tooling-only, Agent Playtest/Webhook/Recorder porting, no reference/system work), mark `Request type: out_of_scope`, decline the 4-role loop, and reroute — do not stretch Analyst/spec templates.

After idea evaluation or a meaningful research/asset close-out, if **rag** is detectable (`RAG_ROOT`, `../rag`, or capture-to-rag defaults), suggest **Capture to RAG: review?** (optional). On approve/immediate capture, run full `capture-to-rag` (including Discord `DISCORD_RAG_WEBHOOK_URL`). Never replace host `docs/` with rag-only logs; never capture secrets; never print webhook URLs.

When working **in the system-crew pack repo** on consumer-facing protocol changes: update `CHANGELOG.md` + bump `VERSION`, then **auto** capture-to-rag (no ask) so hosts can retrieve apply-worthy updates via RAG.

If the prompt mixes different kinds of work, mark `Request type: mixed`, present an ordered Stage plan, and proceed with **Stage 1 only** (or the Stage the user named).

When only long reference-asset drafting remains after decisions are fixed, you may hand that Doc Stage to a **cheap subagent** (e.g. Composer) with a short brief — see `.cursor/system-crew/workflows/cheap-subagent-handoff.md`. Do not offload judgment or invent decisions.
